  "hints": [
    "Place one queen per row `r = 0..n-1` so rows never conflict.",
    "Track blocked columns `cols`, main diagonals `r - c`, and anti-diagonals `r + c` in sets for O(1) conflict checking per candidate square.",
    "Pseudocode:\n  def dfs(r):\n      if r == n: return 1\n      total = 0\n      for c in range(n):\n          if c in cols or (r-c) in diag1 or (r+c) in diag2: continue\n          add; total += dfs(r+1); remove\n      return total"
